   "sfx": "suspicious",
   "text": "A DIFFERENT HOUSE"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "This is a true story, from real records. Borley Rectory, in a village in Essex, England.",
   "cam": "wide",
   "do": [
    [
     "odo",
     "turn:nun"
    ]
   ],
   "text": "BORLEY, ENGLAND"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "One ghost hunter called it the most haunted house in England.",
   "cam": "close:nun",
   "do": [
    [
     "nun",
     "turn:front"
    ]
   ],
   "sfx": "suspicious",
   "text": "MOST HAUNTED HOUSE"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "A vicar, Henry Bull, built it in 1862, right beside the old village church.",
   "cam": "two:odo,moth",
   "do": [
    [
     "moth",
     "turn:front"
    ]
   ],
   "text": "BUILT IN 1862"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "He had fourteen children. So he added a whole new wing.",
   "cam": "wide",
   "do": [
    [
     "odo",
     "jump"
    ]
   ],
   "text": "14 CHILDREN"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "And in that house, people told a story. A story about a nun.",
   "cam": "close:nun",
   "do": [
    [
     "nun",
     "rise"
    ]
   ],
   "sfx": "suspicious",
   "text": "THE NUN"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "The legend said she was locked away near here, long ago. And she never left.",
   "cam": "two:nun,moth",
   "do": [
    [
     "nun",
     "to:4,11"
    ]
   ],
   "text": "SHE NEVER LEFT"
  },
  {
   "who": "moth",
   "say": "Locked away? Odo, I really don't like this story.",
   "cam": "close:moth",
   "do": [
    [
     "moth",
     "shake"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "Historians say the legend was probably made up. But then came one summer evening.",
   "cam": "wide",
   "do": [
    [
     "nun",
     "dive"
    ]
   ],
   "text": "LEGEND... OR NOT?"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "July the twenty-eighth, 1900. Four of the Bull sisters walked in the garden at dusk.",
   "cam": "overhead",
   "do": [
    [
     "odo",
     "to:-3,8"
    ]
   ],
   "text": "28 JULY 1900"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "About forty yards away, they saw a dark figure. A nun, gliding over the grass.",
   "cam": "close:nun",
   "do": [
    [
     "nun",
     "rise"
    ],
    [
     "nun",
     "to:2,12"
    ]
   ],
   "sfx": "alarm",
   "text": "A NUN IN THE GARDEN"
  },
  {
   "who": "odo",
   "say": "Did they run away?",
   "cam": "close:odo",
   "do": [
    [
     "odo",
     "eyes_big"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "One sister walked toward her. And the nun was gone.",
   "cam": "wide",
   "do": [
    [
     "nun",
     "dive"
    ]
   ],
   "sfx": "suspicious",
   "text": "GONE"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "From then on, that path had a name. The Nun's Walk.",
   "cam": "two:odo,moth",
   "do": [
    [
     "moth",
     "turn:odo"
    ]
   ],
   "text": "THE NUN'S WALK"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "In 1928, a new vicar, Guy Smith, moved in with his wife.",
   "cam": "wide",
   "do": [
    [
     "nun",
     "rise"
    ],
    [
     "bell",
     "show"
    ]
   ],
   "text": "1928"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "They heard footsteps in empty rooms. Bells rang by themselves.",
